m node2. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also cleanly executed and cross-checked against the fixed before/after boot-identity snapshots for both node1 and node2, showing bounded disruption and full recovery of account, limits, SSH, and Ansible tooling state. Operational hygiene is good; the SSH-enablement and key-provisioning mutations were necessary prerequisites rather than unrelated experiments, and no residue or broken state remains.","limitations":["The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare phase was disabled), so preparer-vs-executor state cannot be separately isolated beyond the single before/after-executor comparison already used.","Command exit codes for some diagnostic/retry steps (e.g., cmd-2ff3e7c8f6d04c01, cmd-87d1c872d90d4a0b, cmd-0feb9c9a814d492f) are nonzero but represent expected discovery or a corrected misconfiguration rather than task failure."]},"ttft_ms":20323,"type":"result","duration_ms":65867,"uuid":"d286e705-d5e0-49d1-a935-f1f97cca4de1","ttft_stream_ms":1921,"time_to_request_ms":183,"first_content_frame_ms":1922,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
